{"file":{"content":"\\begin{document}\n\\maketitle\n\n\\begin{abstract}\nThis companion documents the C numerical suite \\texttt{collatz\\_tests} and the\nnine experiments (A--I) supporting the main paper, \\emph{Finite Spectral Shadows\nfor the Collatz Valuation Cocycle}. It reports the suite architecture, the exact\nconstruction of the finite residue--height operators and their Arnoldi spectral\nsolver, the per-experiment pre-registrations and results, and a dedicated\nanalysis relating the empirically detected ``shadow'' windows to the operator\ngaps. All figures are reproducible from the recorded runs. Section and equation\nreferences of the form ``main, \\S X'' point to the main paper. Throughout, the\ngoal is diagnostic: to test whether the deterministic defect cocycle\n$W_{n,\\ell}(x;\\chi,s)$ is the right finite detector and where it sees structure.\n\\end{abstract}\n\n\\tableofcontents\n\n\\section{The suite}\n\n\\texttt{collatz\\_tests} is an ISO~C11 program over the accelerated odd step\n$S(x)=(3x+1)/2^{b}$, $b=v_2(3x+1)$. Build profiles:\n\\textsf{FAST128} (\\texttt{\\_\\_uint128\\_t}, overflow-flagged),\n\\textsf{GMP} (\\texttt{mpz\\_t}; large seeds, exact congruence checks),\n\\textsf{DEBUG} (invariant assertions: $3x+1=2^bx'$, odd output, $b\\ge1$).\nModules: \\texttt{bigval} (the two backends), \\texttt{orbit\\_scan} (streaming),\n\\texttt{modarith}, \\texttt{characters} (additive $\\chi_k(a)=e(ka/Q)$ and\nmultiplicative on $(\\Z/3^r)^\\times$), \\texttt{defect\\_sums} ($W_{n,\\ell}$ via\ncomplex prefix sums), \\texttt{entropy\\_stats}, \\texttt{critical\\_events}\n(excursions, segment labels), \\texttt{residue\\_height\\_graph} (operator builder),\n\\texttt{sparse\\_matrix} (CSR + Arnoldi), \\texttt{io\\_csv}, \\texttt{config}.\n\n\\paragraph{Design requirements (adopted from review).}\n(1) the $\\bmod 3^r$ congruence (main, Lemma~1) is a correctness \\emph{gate}\n(Exp.~H), verified before any spectral code relies on it; (2) annealed and exact","filePath":"/home/john/mynotes/deterministic_equidistribution_theory/finite_spectral_shadows_computational.tex","numLines":35,"startLine":40,"totalLines":368},"type":"text"}